IMPORT prelude

-- Protection from Online Falsehoods and Manipulation Act 2019 (Singapore) -- what a "false statement of fact" is (s 2(2)), what
-- "communicated in Singapore" means (s 3), the three Part 2 offences and their penalties (ss 7, 8, 9), when a Part 3 Correction or
-- Stop Communication Direction may be issued to a person (ss 10-12), non-compliance (s 15), appeal and its grounds (s 17), the
-- threshold for declaring an online location (s 32(1)), funding a declared online location (s 38), and composition (s 57).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/POFMA2019.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated in
-- the body is [40/2019]. The retrieval metadata calls it the current version as at 01 Oct 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance to ordinary people in Singapore: anyone who posts, forwards or sells services
-- online can meet it. (An automated count found only 1 of the 527 deposited Singapore Acts citing it by its slug title; that count
-- undercounts and is not a measure of importance.) SCOPED to the provisions an individual poster meets. Not encoded: Part 4
-- directions to internet intermediaries and media (ss 20-31), access blocking orders (ss 16, 28, 33, 34), ss 36-37 beyond mention,
-- Part 6 account restriction directions, Part 7 codes of practice and political advertising, Part 8 alternate authorities in election
-- periods, enforcement powers, offences by corporations, and the s 9(7) uplift.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions (the skill was not loadable in this
-- session; the conventions of the finished example rows were followed). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass,
-- no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Protection from Online Falsehoods and Manipulation Act 2019`

§§ `2(2) -- false statement of fact`

-- s 2(2)(a): "a statement of fact is a statement which a reasonable person seeing, hearing or otherwise perceiving it would consider to
-- be a representation of fact"; (b): "a statement is false if it is false or misleading, whether wholly or in part, and whether on its
-- own or in the context in which it appears".
GIVEN `a reasonable person would take it as a representation of fact` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `wholly or partly false` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `misleading on its own or in context` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a false statement of fact` IF
    `a reasonable person would take it as a representation of fact`
    AND (`wholly or partly false` OR `misleading on its own or in context`)

§§ `3 -- communicated in Singapore`

-- s 3(1): "In this Act other than in Part 2", a statement is communicated in Singapore "if it is made available to one or more
-- end-users in Singapore on or through the internet". (2): "In Part 2", through "(a) the internet; or (b) MMS or SMS". (3): includes
-- causing its communication.
DECLARE Channel IS ONE OF
    `the internet`
    `SMS or MMS`
    `a printed leaflet`

GIVEN `the channel` IS A Channel, `for Part 2` IS A BOOLEAN, `reaches an end-user in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is communicated in Singapore` IF
    `reaches an end-user in Singapore` AND
        (CONSIDER `the channel`
         WHEN `the internet` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `SMS or MMS` THEN `for Part 2`
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `7, 8, 9 -- the Part 2 offences`

-- s 7(1)(b), repeated in ss 8(3) and 9(3): the communication "is likely to" (i) be prejudicial to the security of Singapore; (ii) be
-- prejudicial to public health, public safety, public tranquillity or public finances; (iii) be prejudicial to friendly relations with
-- other countries; (iv) influence the outcome of a Presidential election, general election, by-election or referendum; (v) incite
-- feelings of enmity, hatred or ill-will between different groups; or (vi) diminish public confidence in the Government, an Organ of
-- State or a statutory board.
DECLARE Harm IS ONE OF
    `prejudice to security`
    `prejudice to public health, safety, tranquillity or finances`
    `prejudice to friendly relations`
    `influencing an election or referendum`
    `inciting enmity between groups`
    `diminishing confidence in the Government`
    `no listed harm`

GIVEN `the harm` IS A Harm
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a listed harm` IF
    CONSIDER `the harm`
    WHEN `no listed harm` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 7(1): "A person must not do any act in or outside Singapore in order to communicate in Singapore a statement knowing or having
-- reason to believe that (a) it is a false statement of fact; and (b)" its communication is likely to cause a listed harm.
-- (4): does not apply to acts for or incidental to an internet intermediary service, a telecommunication service, public internet
-- access, or a computing resource service.
GIVEN `acted to communicate it in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or had reason to believe it false` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the harm believed likely` IS A Harm,
      `merely providing an intermediary or carriage service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 7 offence is committed` IF
    `acted to communicate it in Singapore`
    AND `knew or had reason to believe it false`
    AND `it is a listed harm` `the harm believed likely`
    AND (NOT `merely providing an intermediary or carriage service`)

-- s 8(1): a person must not "make or alter a bot with the intention of (a) communicating, by means of the bot, a false statement of
-- fact in Singapore; or (b) enabling any other person to" do so. No listed harm is needed for the offence; a listed harm raises the
-- penalty (s 8(3)).
GIVEN `made or altered a bot` IS A BOOLEAN, `intending it to communicate a falsehood in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 8 offence is committed` IF
    `made or altered a bot` AND `intending it to communicate a falsehood in Singapore`

-- s 9(1): a person who "solicits, receives or agrees to receive any financial or other material benefit as an inducement or reward
-- for providing any service, knowing that the service is or will be used in the communication of one or more false statements of fact
-- in Singapore, shall be guilty of an offence if the service is in fact used in such communication". (4): the same carve-out as s 7(4).
GIVEN `took or agreed to take a benefit for a service` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew it would be used for falsehoods` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the service was in fact so used` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `merely providing an intermediary or carriage service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 9 offence is committed` IF
    `took or agreed to take a benefit for a service`
    AND `knew it would be used for falsehoods`
    AND `the service was in fact so used`
    AND (NOT `merely providing an intermediary or carriage service`)

-- s 9(5): on conviction the court "must ... order the person to pay as a penalty ... a sum equal to the amount of any financial or
-- other material benefit received", recoverable as a fine; (6): not if "the value ... cannot be assessed". (The (7) uplift for
-- offences taken into consideration is not encoded.)
GIVEN `the benefit received` IS A NUMBER, `the value can be assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 9 disgorgement penalty` MEANS
    IF `the value can be assessed` THEN `the benefit received` ELSE 0

§§ `Penalties`

-- s 7(2): individual $50,000 or 5 years or both; otherwise $500,000. s 7(3): where "an inauthentic online account or a bot is used ...
-- for the purpose of accelerating such communication" -- individual $100,000 or 10 years; otherwise $1 million.
-- ss 8(2), 9(2): individual $30,000 or 3 years; otherwise $500,000. ss 8(3), 9(3): where a listed harm is likely -- individual $60,000
-- or 6 years; otherwise $1 million.
-- s 15(1): individual $20,000 or 12 months; otherwise $500,000.
-- s 38(3): individual $40,000 or 3 years; otherwise $500,000.
-- `aggravated` means: for s 7, a bot or inauthentic account used to accelerate; for ss 8 and 9, a listed harm likely. Ignored for
-- ss 15 and 38, which have no aggravated tier.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `communicating a falsehood (s 7)`
    `making a bot for falsehoods (s 8)`
    `providing services for falsehoods (s 9)`
    `ignoring a Part 3 Direction (s 15)`
    `funding a declared online location (s 38)`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `aggravated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `communicating a falsehood (s 7)` THEN
        (IF `an individual` THEN (IF `aggravated` THEN 100000 ELSE 50000)
         ELSE (IF `aggravated` THEN 1000000 ELSE 500000))
    WHEN `making a bot for falsehoods (s 8)` THEN
        (IF `an individual` THEN (IF `aggravated` THEN 60000 ELSE 30000)
         ELSE (IF `aggravated` THEN 1000000 ELSE 500000))
    WHEN `providing services for falsehoods (s 9)` THEN
        (IF `an individual` THEN (IF `aggravated` THEN 60000 ELSE 30000)
         ELSE (IF `aggravated` THEN 1000000 ELSE 500000))
    WHEN `ignoring a Part 3 Direction (s 15)` THEN
        (IF `an individual` THEN 20000 ELSE 500000)
    WHEN `funding a declared online location (s 38)` THEN
        (IF `an individual` THEN 40000 ELSE 500000)

-- Imprisonment is available only "in the case of an individual"; the maximum term in MONTHS.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `aggravated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF NOT `an individual` THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `the offence`
         WHEN `communicating a falsehood (s 7)` THEN (IF `aggravated` THEN 120 ELSE 60)
         WHEN `making a bot for falsehoods (s 8)` THEN (IF `aggravated` THEN 72 ELSE 36)
         WHEN `providing services for falsehoods (s 9)` THEN (IF `aggravated` THEN 72 ELSE 36)
         WHEN `ignoring a Part 3 Direction (s 15)` THEN 12
         WHEN `funding a declared online location (s 38)` THEN 36

§§ `10, 11, 12 -- Part 3 Directions to the person who communicated`

-- s 10(1): any Minister may instruct the Competent Authority to issue a Part 3 Direction if "(a) a false statement of fact ... has been
-- or is being communicated in Singapore; (b) the Minister is of the opinion that it is in the public interest". (2): "even if it has
-- been amended or has ceased to be communicated in Singapore".
-- ss 11(1), 12(1): a Correction or Stop Communication Direction is "issued to a person who communicated the subject statement in
-- Singapore". ss 11(4), 12(4): it may be issued "even if the person does not know or has no reason to believe that the statement is
-- false". ss 11(5)(b), 12(7)(c): a person does not communicate "merely by" providing an intermediary or carriage service.
-- Outside Part 2, "communicated in Singapore" means through the internet only (s 3(1)) -- so an SMS falsehood is not reached here.
GIVEN `it is a false statement of fact` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person made it available online to Singapore end-users` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `merely providing an intermediary or carriage service` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Minister thinks it in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person knew it was false` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it has since been taken down` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Part 3 Direction may be issued to the person` IF
    `it is a false statement of fact`
    AND `the person made it available online to Singapore end-users`
    AND (NOT `merely providing an intermediary or carriage service`)
    AND `the Minister thinks it in the public interest`

§§ `15 -- failing to comply with a Part 3 Direction`

-- s 15(1): a person "to whom a Part 3 Direction is issued and served and who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply". (2): "It is
-- not a defence" that a written law, rule of law, contract or professional rule prevents compliance, or that the person "has applied
-- under section 19 to vary or cancel" or "has appealed". s 19(3): the Direction "remains in effect despite any application".
GIVEN `issued and served` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has applied to vary or appealed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a contract forbids compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 15 offence is committed` IF
    `issued and served`
    AND `failed to comply`
    AND (NOT `has a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `17 -- appeal to the General Division of the High Court`

-- s 17(2): "No appeal may be made ... unless the person has first applied to the Minister mentioned in section 19 to vary or cancel the
-- Part 3 Direction ... and the Minister refused the application whether in whole or in part."
GIVEN `applied to the Minister to vary or cancel` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister refused in whole or part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal to the High Court may be made` IF
    `applied to the Minister to vary or cancel` AND `the Minister refused in whole or part`

-- s 17(5): the court "may only set aside a Part 3 Direction on any of the following grounds": (a) the person did not communicate the
-- subject statement in Singapore; (b) it "is not a statement of fact, or is a true statement of fact"; (c) "it is not technically
-- possible to comply". The Minister's public-interest opinion and the person's state of knowledge are not listed.
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `the appellant did not communicate it in Singapore`
    `it is not a statement of fact`
    `it is a true statement of fact`
    `compliance is technically impossible`
    `issuing it was not in the public interest`
    `the appellant did not know it was false`
    `compliance would breach a contract`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may set aside on that ground` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `issuing it was not in the public interest` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the appellant did not know it was false` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `compliance would breach a contract` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 17(6): the Direction "remains in effect despite the appeal" until set aside, expired or cancelled. (7): but if the appellant
-- "establishes a prima facie case that it is technically impossible to comply", the court "may direct that the Direction be stayed".
GIVEN `has appealed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `set aside, expired or cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `stayed by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Direction must still be complied with` IF
    (NOT `set aside, expired or cancelled`) AND (NOT `stayed by the court`)

GIVEN `has appealed` IS A BOOLEAN, `prima facie case of technical impossibility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may stay the Direction` IF
    `has appealed` AND `prima facie case of technical impossibility`

§§ `32(1) -- declared online locations`

-- s 32(1): the Minister may declare an online location if "(a) 3 or more different statements that are the subject of one or more
-- active Part 3 Directions or Part 4 Directions ... have been or are being communicated in Singapore on the online location; (b) at
-- least 3 of those statements had first been communicated in Singapore on the online location within 6 months before" the
-- Declaration. (3)(d): expiry "must not be later than 2 years after" it comes into effect.
GIVEN `different statements under active Directions` IS A NUMBER, `of them first posted in the last 6 months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the location may be declared` IF
    `different statements under active Directions` AT LEAST 3
    AND `of them first posted in the last 6 months` AT LEAST 3

§§ `38 -- funding a declared online location`

-- s 38(1): a person must not "expend or apply any property knowing or having reason to believe that the expenditure or application
-- supports, helps or promotes the communication of false statements of fact in Singapore on a declared online location". (2): does
-- not apply to a service provider or digital advertising intermediary giving consideration "for the purpose of communicating any paid
-- content" there (those are dealt with by s 37). (4): "property" includes money.
GIVEN `spent money or property on it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or had reason to believe it supports falsehoods on a declared location` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an ad service provider or intermediary paying for paid content` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 38 offence is committed` IF
    `spent money or property on it`
    AND `knew or had reason to believe it supports falsehoods on a declared location`
    AND (NOT `an ad service provider or intermediary paying for paid content`)

§§ `57 -- composition`

-- s 57(1): an authorised officer may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting ... a sum not exceeding
-- one half of the amount of the maximum fine". Which offences are prescribed is in regulations not retrieved.
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `its maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    IF `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` THEN `its maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2 ELSE 0
